<p>NOTE: Net loss for the first quarter 1997 included special charges totalling $17.6 million ($11.2 million, net of tax) for impaired long-lived assets and to adjust carrying values of under-performing restaurants to estimated fair market value.  The charge was based on a review of the company's restaurants in connection with the adoption of Financial Accounting Standard No. 121.  Excluding the effects of the FAS 121 charge, the company's loss from continuing operations was $2.6 million or $(.05) per share.</p>
